        "narration": "Eleanor's preserved correspondence describes numb lips after her nightly medicine and plants dying when she poured it into their pots. Her diary says, \"S. knows that I know. He watches me drink every night.\" With the letters is an account of false prescriptions and two patients who died. Eleanor had intended to tell Ambrose. Ashgrove signed her death certificate as fever.\n\nAmbrose's written instructions to the medium are found: ask, \"Who gave me the tonic?\" He paid for a trap, not a genuine spirit. A note from his coat says, \"Watch S.A.'s hands when the lights return.\" The withheld codicil directs attention to the signer of Eleanor's death certificate. The records are now on the table for these guests to compare.\n\nNow read the new clues. Documents supply a reason to fear this gathering. The final task is still to connect that fear to the movements around Ambrose's glass.\n\n{wren} reads Eleanor's preserved diary and correspondence. {marsh} opens the codicil and reads its instruction. {vesper} reads the written seance question.\nWhy did Ambrose arrange this gathering? In this 16-player edition, the comparison passes through the whole table:\n{ashgrove} leads the comparison concerning {marsh}.\n{crane} leads the comparison concerning {pell}.\n{constance} leads the comparison concerning {finch}.\n{vesper} leads the comparison concerning {wren}.\n{grey} leads the comparison concerning {ivy}.\n{marsh} leads the comparison concerning {vane}.\n{pell} leads the comparison concerning {blackwood}.\n{finch} leads the comparison concerning {mourner1}.\n{wren} leads the comparison concerning {mourner2}.\n{ivy} leads the comparison concerning {mourner3}.\n{vane} leads the comparison concerning {mourner4}.\n{blackwood} leads the comparison concerning {ashgrove}.\n{mourner1} leads the comparison concerning {crane}.\n{mourner2} leads the comparison concerning {constance}.\n{mourner3} leads the comparison concerning {vesper}.\n{mourner4} leads the comparison concerning {grey}.\nEvery guest reads the findings below on their phone; nobody acts out a discovery.",
