        "narration": "Place the evidence in order. Before tonight, Eleanor recorded harm from medicine and threatened to expose the prescription accounts. Tonight Ambrose brought the bottle and hired the performance to ask about it. During the blackout, a chair scraped, a ringed hand reached toward his glass, and he died. The poison was on that glass alone.\n\nThe final comparison adds the glove observation: Ashgrove removed his gloves before the seance and replaced them when the lights returned. It is a witness detail to test against the ring account, not a confession. His immediate weak-heart explanation must also be weighed against the poison symptoms, handwriting and soil.\n\nRead every final clue. Other guests have debts and wrongdoing, but do those explain both deaths and this method? Name a suspect from the evidence already spoken, not from a secret packet or a supernatural answer.\n\n{blackwood} reads the glove observation for the final comparison. {wren} returns to Eleanor's warning. {ashgrove} reads the sequence linking tonic, blackout and glass.\nWhose account explains both deaths? In this 16-player edition, the comparison passes through the whole table:\n{ashgrove} leads the comparison concerning {ivy}.\n{crane} leads the comparison concerning {vane}.\n{constance} leads the comparison concerning {blackwood}.\n{vesper} leads the comparison concerning {mourner1}.\n{grey} leads the comparison concerning {mourner2}.\n{marsh} leads the comparison concerning {mourner3}.\n{pell} leads the comparison concerning {mourner4}.\n{finch} leads the comparison concerning {ashgrove}.\n{wren} leads the comparison concerning {crane}.\n{ivy} leads the comparison concerning {constance}.\n{vane} leads the comparison concerning {vesper}.\n{blackwood} leads the comparison concerning {grey}.\n{mourner1} leads the comparison concerning {marsh}.\n{mourner2} leads the comparison concerning {pell}.\n{mourner3} leads the comparison concerning {finch}.\n{mourner4} leads the comparison concerning {wren}.\nEvery guest reads the findings below on their phone; nobody acts out a discovery.",
