        "title": "Round 4 - The Drink That Did Not Kill",
        "narration": "The remaining brandy and the fragments of Ambrose's glass are compared. The decanter has no wolfsbane residue; the individual glass rim does. Constance drank from the same decanter and survived. Pouring the drinks is not the same as touching one rim during the blackout.\n\nThe doorway account describes a serpent-and-staff ring on the reaching hand. Ashgrove wears that physician's ring. Finch develops the photograph and places it beside the doorway account. Both describe the same ring; compare them instead of trusting a single witness. The medium's script explains the false haunting. It does not explain the poisoned glass. The stolen candlestick explains Crane's doorway movement without making him an innocent witness by decree.\n\nKeep the earlier accusations beside these corrections. Ask which explanation fits the bottle, the shared drink and the single poisoned rim without changing any of those facts.\n\n{finch} compares the ring account with the glass findings. {constance} places her shared drink beside the decanter comparison. {vesper} matches the performance account to Ambrose's instructions.\nWhich accusation survives the clean decanter? In this 22-player edition, the comparison passes through the whole table:\n{ashgrove} leads the comparison concerning {finch}.\n{crane} leads the comparison concerning {wren}.\n{constance} leads the comparison concerning {ivy}.\n{vesper} leads the comparison concerning {vane}.\n{grey} leads the comparison concerning {blackwood}.\n{marsh} leads the comparison concerning {mourner1}.\n{pell} leads the comparison concerning {mourner2}.\n{finch} leads the comparison concerning {mourner3}.\n{wren} leads the comparison concerning {mourner4}.\n{ivy} leads the comparison concerning {mourner5}.\n{vane} leads the comparison concerning {mourner6}.\n{blackwood} leads the comparison concerning {mourner7}.\n{mourner1} leads the comparison concerning {mourner8}.\n{mourner2} leads the comparison concerning {mourner9}.\n{mourner3} leads the comparison concerning {mourner10}.\n{mourner4} leads the comparison concerning {ashgrove}.\n{mourner5} leads the comparison concerning {crane}.\n{mourner6} leads the comparison concerning {constance}.\n{mourner7} leads the comparison concerning {vesper}.\n{mourner8} leads the comparison concerning {grey}.\n{mourner9} leads the comparison concerning {marsh}.\n{mourner10} leads the comparison concerning {pell}.\nEvery guest reads the findings below on their phone; nobody acts out a discovery.",
