      "explanation": "Ashgrove is the only suspect connecting both deaths. Eleanor's preserved papers describe harmful tonic, false prescriptions and her intention to expose them; his handwriting is on the bottle and he certified fever. Ambrose kept those records and hired a staged seance to ask about the tonic. During its blackout, the account of a reaching hand identifies the physician's serpent-and-staff ring. The poison was on Ambrose's glass rim, not in the decanter Constance drank from. The cut monkshood, soil and glove observation corroborate the method and opportunity. Debts, thefts and the fraudulent performance explain other suspicious acts, but not this whole chain. No supernatural confession or private clue is needed.",
